-- title:
--   Noetherian local ring of dimension two on the plane model
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, let $k$ be a field of characteristic $q$, let $\mathrm{red}\colon A\to k$ be a ring homomorphism and $a\in k$, and let $K$ be a finite extension of $\mathbb Q$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$. Write $A_0=\mathtt{coeffSubring}\,A\,K=A\cap K$ for the subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ obtained by intersecting $A$ with $K$, and $\mathrm{red}_0=\mathtt{redRestrict}\,\mathrm{red}\,K$ for the composite of the inclusion $A_0\hookrightarrow A$ with $\mathrm{red}$. Assume given $x\in A_0$ with $\mathrm{red}_0(x)=a$, and $\varpi\in A_0$ such that for all $c\in A_0$ one has $\mathrm{red}_0(c)=0$ if and only if $c\in\varpi A_0$. Let $R_0=\mathtt{modularLocalizedAtPoint}\,(1\cdot q)\,A_0\,\mathrm{red}_0\,a\,(a^q)$ be the subring of the Laurent series field over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ consisting of those $f$ for which there are $r,s\in A_0[X_0,X_1]$ with $s(a,a^q)\neq 0$ after applying $\mathrm{red}_0$ to coefficients, and $f\cdot s(\mathtt{jqModC},\mathtt{jqNModC}\,(1\cdot q))=r(\mathtt{jqModC},\mathtt{jqNModC}\,(1\cdot q))$, where evaluation $\mathtt{modularEval}$ sends coefficients to constant series, $X_0$ to the $q$-expansion $\mathtt{jqModC}$ of $j$ and $X_1$ to its $\mathtt{qExpand}$-transform $\mathtt{jqNModC}\,(1\cdot q)$. Then $R_0$ is a noetherian ring, is a local ring, has $\mathtt{ringKrullDim}\,R_0=2$, and its maximal ideal is the ideal generated by the three elements of $R_0$ given by the $\mathtt{modularEval}$-images of $\varpi$, of $X_0-x$ and of $X_1-x^q$ (the last conjunct being stated for an arbitrary local-ring instance on $R_0$).
--
--   This identifies the local ring at a point of the characteristic-$q$ fibre of the plane model of $X_0(q)$ cut out by the pair $(j,j_q)$ of $q$-expansions, together with a generating set of its maximal ideal: a localisation of $A_0[X_0,X_1]$ with $A_0$ a discrete valuation ring in the relevant case. It is used in the node-descent analysis of this model, for instance in the existence and uniqueness statements for places centred at the cusps or at $j=1728$ arising from a crossing presentation.
-- source:
